      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the ROCE formula?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "ROCE = (EBIT / Capital Employed) x 100. Capital Employed = Total Assets - Current Liabilities, which is equivalent to Shareholders' Equity + Long-term Debt. EBIT is earnings before interest and tax, taken from the income statement. Total Assets and Current Liabilities come from the balance sheet." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
